      "text": "Since the triangles are similar, the ratio of their perimeters is the same as the ratio of their corresponding sides.\nLet $x$ be the length of the longest side of the similar triangle.\nThe ratio of the perimeters is $\\frac{110}{\\text{perimeter of original triangle}}$.\nSince the original triangle's perimeter is $6+7+9=22$, this ratio is $\\frac{110}{22}=\\frac{5}{1}$.\nSince the ratio of the perimeters is equal to the ratio of the corresponding sides,\nthe ratio of the longest side to the original triangle's longest side is $\\frac{5}{1}$.\nSince the longest side of the original triangle has length 9 cm, the longest side of the similar triangle has length $9\\times\\frac{5}{1}=\\boxed{45}$ centimeters.\nThe answer is: 45",
